          "title": "You'll want to know: माप",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माप — māp — \"a size; a measure\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ये जूती म्हारो माप कोनी। ye jūtī mhāro māp konī. These shoes aren't my size."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माप (māp) is inherited from Sanskrit māpya, \"to be measured\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry, but lists Hindi māp, \"measurement, measure\" (CDIAL 10053)."
            }
          ]
        },
